#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Agincourt: between the woods of Azincourt and Tramecourt, 25 October
1415.  A sample game for the Grognard engine.

Henry V of England has taken Harfleur and is marching his sick and
hungry army to Calais.  The army of France has got in front of him,
three or four times his number, and on Saint Crispin's day he must
fight his way through or starve.  His men-at-arms stand on foot in a
thin line across a ploughed field soaked by a night of rain, his
archers on the wings and between the battles behind sharpened stakes,
and the woods on either side close in so that the French can't go round.
Play either side against the computer, or against a friend at the same
screen.

Run it with ./agincourt (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.agincourt.json.  ./agincourt --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

